%N A398593 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * H(2*k)^2/k^2, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number.
%H A398593 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.53, pp. 450-451, eq. (4.179), section 5.53, p. 468, section 6.53, pp. 770-779.
%H A398593 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398593 Equals 2*G^2 - log(2)*Pi*G + 231*zeta(4)/32 - 35*log(2)*zeta(3)/16 + log(2)^2*zeta(2) - 5*log(2)^4/48 - 2*Pi*Im(Li_3((1+i)/2)) - 5*Li_4(1/2)/2, where G is Catalan's constant (A006752), and i is the imaginary unit.
%e A398593 1.564451262854388978464001544660529094843728442334648...
%t A398593 RealDigits[2*Catalan^2 - Log[2]*Pi*Catalan + 231*Zeta[4]/32 - 35*Log[2]*Zeta[3]/16 + Log[2]^2*Zeta[2] - 5*Log[2]^4/48 - 2*Pi*Im[PolyLog[3, (1 + I)/2]] - 5*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/2, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398593 (PARI) 2*Catalan^2 - log(2)*Pi*Catalan + 231*zeta(4)/32 - 35*log(2)*zeta(3)/16 + log(2)^2*zeta(2) - 5*log(2)^4/48 - 2*Pi*imag(polylog(3, (1+I)/2)) - 5*polylog(4, 1/2)/2
